\nIt matters that the rule uses the largest *connected object*, not the most frequent colour. In pair 1, colour 1 has 95 cells in total and would win a frequency count. Those cells are split into many small pieces, though, so it never forms the biggest single object. The rule is therefore: **find the largest single-colour connected object and fill a 3×3 grid with its colour.**\n\n**Applying it to the test.** The largest object is the colour-5 blob with 39 cells. The next largest are the colour-6 and colour-8 objects with 19 cells each. The expected output is a 3×3 grid of 5s.\n\n**Construction stages.** The program emits two canvases:\n1. The 3×3 output allocated and filled with the background colour.\n2. The same canvas filled with the colour of the largest object, which is the final answer.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    biggest = max(objs, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])\n    out = np.full((3, 3), bg, dtype=int)\n    emit(out, \"Allocate the 3x3 output canvas (background colour).\")\n    out[:, :] = biggest[\"colour\"]\n    emit(out, f\"Fill it with colour {biggest['colour']}, the colour of the largest \"\n              f\"connected object ({biggest['size']} cells).\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Which colour is chosen.** The fact sheet lists the connected objects (4-connected, same colour) from largest to smallest:"}],"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"hich colour is chosen.** The fact sheet lists the connected objects (4-connected, same colour) from largest to smallest:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1: the largest object is colour 3 with 28 cells."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 2: the largest object is colour 4 with 25 cells."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 1, colour 1 has 95 cells in total and would win a frequency count."}],"crop":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate the 3x3 output canvas (background colour)."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"On top of the noise sit a few solid blobs, each in a single colour: 3, 5, 4 and 9 in pair 1."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"5fc1f078ee317d27991799cf4eed3b42960e2435a843f2ad313d37ec9a07f617","task_sha256":"84a8e54cbe53ad2c033b4ec8f137fd59bde98df27f72a3f5aff569aebf50e4e1","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
